Installer licences and sources

Each release provides two downloads with the same version number.

The installer download, hello-guix-VERSION.tar.gz, extracts to hello-guix/.
Inside that folder, COPYING explains Hello Guix’s licensing, LICENSES/
holds the licence texts, and notices/ contains upstream licences and
credits. Python, Tcl and Tk also retain licence files under runtime/.
Packages inside the Guix image retain their own terms.

The matching source download, hello-guix-VERSION-src.tar.gz, extracts to
hello-guix-VERSION-src/. The project source is at the top of this folder,
with build instructions in docs/development.md. Sources for Asahi’s
installer, the macOS runtime and the Guix image are under upstream/.

All paths above refer to the extracted downloads. Apple’s device firmware
is collected from the target Mac during installation and is not included
in either download.
